<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Paris-Mexico plane diverted to Ireland after scare.</title>
<headline>Paris-Mexico plane diverted to Ireland after scare.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Air France flight from Paris to Mexico was diverted to Ireland's Shannon airport on Thursday after a bomb scare, Irish radio reported.</p>
<p>It said the aircraft was expected in Shannon, a transatlantic terminus on Ireland's West coast, shortly. Officials at Shannon airport declined all comment. reuter ajh</p>
